
.main__menu
  absolute left 0 right 0 top 0 bottom 0
  overflow-y scroll
  display flex
  flex-direction column

.menu__icon
  display inline-block
  fill currentColor
  vertical-align middle

// THE THREE MENU BUTTONS ARE ONE FAMILY IN THREE TIERS — filled, outlined,
// bare — and they now speak the prose language (app/styles/prose-form.styl)
// rather than imitating Material. What they carried until 2026-08-16 was MUI's
// default primary (#1976d2) and its dark variant, its three-layer elevation
// shadow, its standard easing curve (0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), its Button typography
// down to the seven-decimal 0.02857em tracking, and its FAB geometry: a 24px
// pill and a 40px circle. None of those five appears anywhere else on this
// site, and there was no MUI component underneath any of it.
//
// THE FLOATING BUTTON'S REAL CONSTRAINT IS THAT IT FLOATS OVER EVERYTHING —
// tables, the auction, the players list and the prose pages, all on the same
// #f0f0f0 surface. That is exactly what makes $prose_ink the one paint that
// works: a filled ink rectangle is the darkest thing on the surface, so it
// neither washes out nor shouts. Every lighter treatment fails — an outlined
// or white button dissolves into the surface — and the accent red is the site's
// ONE accent, which cannot be spent on a control that is on screen at all
// times. The accent goes on HOVER instead, which is what prose_action_fill()
// already does for the landing call to action and for every prose submit
// button.
//
// prose_action_fill() itself is deliberately not called here. Half of it fits
// and half does not: a floating action button carries fixed positioning, a
// shadow, an icon slot and label-scale type, so calling the mixin would emit
// four declarations this rule immediately overrides. It is the same paint,
// named from the same variables, rather than a shim over the mixin.
.main__menu-button
  position fixed
  // POSITION LIVES HERE, NOT IN A STYLE OBJECT. menu.js used to set bottom and
  // left/right inline, and an inline style beats a stylesheet rule — so the
  // .auction__live offsets at the foot of this file could never apply and the
  // button sat over the auction controls. The side is a media query rather
  // than a JS width test for the same class of reason: the old isMobile was
  // read once at render with no resize listener, so the button stayed on the
  // wrong edge until something else re-rendered it.
  bottom 16px
  left 16px
  display inline-flex
  align-items center
  // 38px and 14/16px of padding, down from 46px and 24/26px. This control is on
  // screen at ALL times on every page, and the label is five characters at 11px
  // -- the old box was mostly air, and on a phone that air sits on top of
  // content the layout cannot move out from under it.
  height 38px
  // The label is the whole control — there is no hamburger beside it. A mark
  // and a word both saying "menu" is the same thing twice, and at label scale
  // the glyph was the larger of the two, so the word was arguing with an icon
  // that outweighed it.
  //
  // Asymmetric on purpose: the wide tracking below leaves a trailing space
  // after the final letter, which sits the label left of the button's centre
  // under equal padding. THE GAP STAYS 2px WHATEVER THE PADDING IS, because it
  // answers the trailing space rather than the box: `letter-spacing 0.16em` at
  // `font-size 11px` is 1.76px, so 2px is the correction at any size. Scaling
  // the asymmetry down with the padding would have under-corrected it.
  padding 0 14px 0 16px
  border none
  border-radius 3px
  // $prose_action, the same graphite as the landing call to action and every
  // prose submit — a filled block wants a lighter paint than a letterform, so
  // this is deliberately not the near-black $prose_ink.
  background $prose_action
  color $prose_paper
  // The site's label voice — prose_eyebrow()'s mono at small size with wide
  // tracking — rather than MUI Button's sans at 14px. Uppercase survives the
  // rewrite because it belongs to both languages; the face, the size and the
  // tracking are what separated them.
  font-family $prose_mono
  font-size 11px
  font-weight $prose_bold
  letter-spacing 0.16em
  text-transform uppercase
  cursor pointer
  z-index $z_floating_action
  // ONE layer, not Material's three. The contrast against both surfaces is
  // already doing the separating, so the shadow only has to lift the object
  // off the page.
  box-shadow 0 6px 20px rgba(23, 24, 26, 0.18)
  transition background 120ms ease, box-shadow 120ms ease, transform 120ms ease
  &:hover
    background $prose_accent
    box-shadow 0 8px 24px rgba(193, 18, 31, 0.24)
  &:active
    transform translateY(1px)
  // Ink rather than the accent ring the other two get, because THIS button
  // repaints to the accent on hover — an accent ring on an accent fill is no
  // ring at all for anyone who tabs to a button the pointer is resting on. The
  // offset leaves a gap of surface showing, so the ring reads in every state:
  // against the graphite fill, against the accent one, and against the page.
  &:focus-visible
    outline 2px solid $prose_ink
    outline-offset 3px

// TIER THREE, bare. The quietest control in the menu: an info affordance
// beside a warning, which should not read as a button until it is reached for.
// It had no focus style at all before.
.menu__icon-button
  display inline-flex
  align-items center
  justify-content center
  width 24px
  height 24px
  padding 0
  margin 0 0 0 4px
  border none
  border-radius 3px
  background transparent
  color $prose_muted
  cursor pointer
  transition color 120ms ease
  &:hover
    color $prose_accent
  &:focus-visible
    outline 2px solid $prose_accent
    outline-offset 2px

// TIER TWO, outlined. It closes the menu it sits in, so it is an exit rather
// than the point of the surface — filling it would put two solid ink blocks on
// screen at once and make the drawer argue with the button that opened it. A
// square at the family's 3px radius, not Material's 40px circle.
.menu__collapse-button
  display inline-flex
  align-items center
  justify-content center
  width 36px
  height 36px
  padding 0
  border 1px solid $prose_rule_strong
  border-radius 3px
  background transparent
  color $prose_ink
  cursor pointer
  transition border-color 120ms ease, color 120ms ease
  &:hover
    border-color $prose_ink
    color $prose_accent
  &:focus-visible
    outline 2px solid $prose_accent
    outline-offset 2px

.league__menu
  display flex
  padding-left 32px
  position relative

.league__title
  font-family 'IBM Plex Mono'
  font-size 21px
  padding-bottom 8px
  display flex
  justify-content center
  padding 16px 8px

// The league title, as a disclosure. The summary carries the SAME typography as
// the static .league__title above, so a manager in one league and a manager in
// three see the same heading — one of them just has a chevron on it. Only the
// accordion's own 14px prose-sans defaults are overridden.
//
// The name WRAPS here, which is the whole reason this is not a select: nothing
// in the chain reports an intrinsic width, so a long league name costs lines
// rather than pushing the drawer wider.
.league__switcher
  .accordion__summary
    font-family 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace
    font-size 21px
    font-weight 400
    line-height 1.2
    padding 16px 8px
    gap 8px
    // The accordion centres its row because its own summaries are one line.
    // A league name here takes up to four in a 176px card, and a chevron
    // parked halfway down that block reads as unattached to anything. Both
    // children go to the top so the chevron sits on the first line, where the
    // affordance belongs.
    align-items flex-start

  .accordion__summary-content
    align-items flex-start

  // The chevron's own box is taller than one line of 21px, so it needs nudging
  // back onto the cap height rather than sitting above it.
  .accordion__chevron
    margin-top 2px

  .accordion__details
    padding 0 0 8px

// EVERY ANCHOR HERE IS A FLEX BOX, inherited from .menu__links, and a flex item
// takes `min-width: auto` — so a league name with no space to break at would
// report its whole width as a minimum and widen the drawer past its 240px, the
// exact defect this switcher already shipped once with a select. `min-width 0`
// removes that floor and `overflow-wrap anywhere` gives the text somewhere to
// break when there is no space to break at.
.league__switcher-list
  margin-top 0
  a
    min-width 0
    overflow-wrap anywhere

.menu__collapse
  position absolute
  // Tucked into the drawer's own left corner, so it sits under the section
  // cards rather than in the seam beside them.
  left 4px
  bottom 16px

.menu__sections
  flex 1 0 auto
  display flex
  flex-wrap wrap
  align-content flex-start
  padding 14px
  font-family 'Inter', sans-serif

.menu__backdrop
  position fixed
  inset 0
  background rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)
  z-index $z_overlay_backdrop
  -webkit-tap-highlight-color transparent

.menu__drawer
  position fixed
  top var(--app-banner-height, 0px)
  bottom 0
  width $menuWidth
  // The same surface the app body sits on, so the drawer reads as part of the
  // page rather than as a panel laid over it. Deliberately no seam border down
  // the right edge: the section cards are what mark the drawer's extent, and a
  // rule there just draws attention to a join the matching surface exists to
  // hide.
  background $backgroundColor
  z-index $z_overlay_panel
  overflow hidden
  display flex
  flex-direction column
  transition transform 225ms cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1)
  .menu__sections
    max-width 1100px
    margin 0 auto
    padding 16px 24px

.menu__drawer--persistent
  left 0
  transform translateX(-100%)
  &.menu__drawer--open
    transform translateX(0)

.menu__drawer--temporary
  transform translateX(100%)
  right 0
  &.menu__drawer--open
    transform translateX(0)

.menu__section
  border-radius 4px
  min-width 136px
  // Now that the drawer carries the body surface, the cards are the only thing
  // in here that reads as chrome, so they take paper to sit off it.
  background $prose_paper
  flex 1
  margin 8px
  transition background-color $smooth_transition,box-shadow $smooth_transition,border $smooth_transition

.menu__links
  margin-top 8px
  padding-bottom 8px
  a
    display flex
    align-items center
    padding 3px 16px
    font-weight 400
    font-size 12px
    line-height 16px
    &.active
      font-weight 900
      color red

.menu__heading
  padding 16px 16px 0
  font-weight 600
  text-transform capitalize
  font-family 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace
  display flex
  align-items center
  .team__image
    margin 4px
    width 30px
    height 30px

.menu__text
  font-family 'Montserrat', sans-serif
  font-size 32px
  letter-spacing 0.1em
  margin 48px auto 32px
  transition color $smooth_transition,box-shadow $smooth_transition

.menu__open .main__menu-button
  display none

.league__warning
  display flex
  align-items center
  justify-content center
  background-color rgb(255, 244, 229)
  padding 6px
  font-size 10px

// THE AUCTION HAS THREE ZONES, NOT TWO, and this button is the one control that
// has to know about all three. They are set by 1160 and 800:
//
//   >= 1160  the bid bar is a single 70px row, capped at 1120px and centred;
//            the side rail is beside the board. Chrome is $auctionHeightDesktop.
//   801-1159 the bar STACKS, because below the cap it gets the viewport and the
//            actions row is a fixed 551px, leaving the player half 233px at 1024
//            and 29px at 820. The rail is still beside the board.
//   <= 800   the bar is stacked AND the rail has stacked under it, so the button
//            has a rail to clear as well as the chrome.
//
// 1160 is not a new number — it is where the bar already gained its
// `max-width 1120px` cap, and the cap is exactly the condition under which the
// single row fits. auction-controls.styl, page.styl and
// auction-commissioner-controls.styl move with it or the chrome and the page
// disagree about where the chrome ends.
@media (min-width 1160px)
  .auction__live .main__menu-button
    bottom $auctionHeightDesktop + 8px

@media (max-width 1159px)
  .auction__live .main__menu-button
    bottom $auctionHeightMobile + 8px

@media (max-width 800px)
  // The drawer comes in from the right on a phone, so the button that opens it
  // sits on that edge too — and under the thumb rather than across the screen
  // from it. Same specificity as the base rule, so it wins on source order.
  .main__menu-button
    left auto
    right 16px

  // CLEARS THE WHOLE SIDE RAIL, not just the auction chrome, and ONLY in this
  // zone — above 800 the rail is beside the board rather than under it, and the
  // button is on the left edge anyway. Stacked, the rail sits between the chrome
  // and the board and it DOES NOT SCROLL — measured at 768, 600 and 400 it is
  // exactly its three rows with no slack, so any offset that leaves the button
  // inside it covers a row that can never be moved out from under it. At the old
  // $auctionHeightMobile + 8px that row was the standing elections summary, and
  // 83% of its disclosure chevron.
  //
  // The rail's height is not a constant — 115px at 768, 145px at 400, and the
  // settlement status inside it names every team still to answer, so it grows
  // with the league. auction.js measures it and publishes
  // --auction-side-height; the fallback of 0px degrades to the rule above rather
  // than to something wild if the property is ever missing.
  //
  // MUST STAY BELOW the max-width 1159px rule: both are 0,2,0 and the cascade
  // decides on source order, so reordering these silently drops the rail term.
  .auction__live .main__menu-button
    bottom s(
      'calc(%s + var(--auction-side-height, 0px) + 8px)',
      $auctionHeightMobile
    )

@media (pointer: fine)
  .menu__links a:hover
  a.menu__text:hover
    color red
  .main__menu a:hover
    background-color rgba(0,0,0,0.08)
  .menu__section:hover
    // The lift itself is shared — see hover_lift() in app/styles/variables.styl,
    // which the flat button now calls too. The border edge stays here because it
    // is this surface's own, not part of the effect.
    border-color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.23)
    hover_lift()

// The three buttons above are the only things in this file that move on their
// own. The drawer's own slide is untouched here, since it predates this rule.
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)
  .main__menu-button
  .menu__icon-button
  .menu__collapse-button
    transition none
  .main__menu-button:active
    transform none

@media (max-width 500px)
  .menu__links a
    font-size 14px
    line-height 18px
    min-height 36px

@media (pointer: coarse)
  .menu__links a
    font-size 14px
    line-height 18px
    min-height 36px
